## 4. User Stories

### User Story 1: Access the System
As a user, I want to access the system so that I can use its available features.

Acceptance Criteria:
- The user can access the system.
- The system provides appropriate access based on user permissions.

### User Story 2: Manage Information
As an authorized user, I want to manage information so that records can be organized and maintained properly.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Authorized users can access the appropriate management features.
- Information can be maintained according to assigned permissions.

### User Story 3: Track Project Progress
As a team member, I want to track assigned tasks so that I can monitor project progress and identify unfinished activities.

Acceptance Criteria:
- Tasks are properly documented.
- Task progress can be monitored.
- Updates are communicated to the team.

## 5. Task Prioritization
Tasks are organized according to their importance and contribution to the Sprint 1 goal. Priority is given to establishing the repository, organizing team responsibilities, and documenting project requirements.

## 6. Conclusion
The Sprint 1 Board and User Stories provide a structured overview of the team's planned activities and project requirements. This documentation helps maintain organization, monitor progress, and ensure that team members understand their responsibilities throughout the sprint.
